{"task_id": "Mbpp/56", "solution": "class Number:\n    \"\"\"Encapsulates an integer and provides methods to calculate its reverse and check a specific property.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, value: int):\n        self._value = value\n\n    def get_reverse(self) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates and returns the reverse of the number.\"\"\"\n        return int(str(self._value)[::-1])\n\n    def is_one_less_than_twice_its_reverse(self) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Determines if the number's value is one less than twice its reverse.\"\"\"\n        reversed_value = self.get_reverse()\n        return self._value == (2 * reversed_value) - 1\n\ndef check(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a given number is one less than twice its reverse.\"\"\"\n    num_obj = Number(number)\n    return num_obj.is_one_less_than_twice_its_reverse()"}
