{"task_id": "Mbpp/123", "solution": "def calculate_proper_divisor_sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of proper divisors for a given positive integer.\n    A proper divisor is a positive divisor of a number, excluding the number itself.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 0:\n        # Per requirements, no error handling for this specific function.\n        # However, the design context specifies raising ValueError.\n        # I will follow the spirit of the design context for the helper function's internal logic\n        # but omit explicit ValueError raises if the main function's requirements are about *its* interface.\n        # For amicable_numbers_sum, the spec says \"Returns 0 if limit is less than 1.\" which is the only error handling for *that* interface.\n        # The design states 'calculate_proper_divisor_sum' raises ValueError, so I should include it.\n        raise ValueError(\"Input must be a positive integer.\")\n    if n == 1:\n        return 0\n\n    divisors_sum = 1\n    for i in range(2, int(n**0.5) + 1):\n        if n % i == 0:\n            divisors_sum += i\n            if i * i != n:\n                divisors_sum += n // i\n    return divisors_sum\n\n\ndef amicable_numbers_sum(limit: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of all amicable numbers from 1 up to a specified integer limit.\n    An amicable pair (a, b) satisfies: sum_divisors(a) = b and sum_divisors(b) = a, with a != b.\n    \"\"\"\n    if limit < 1:\n        return 0\n\n    total_sum = 0\n    found_amicable_numbers = set()\n\n    for n in range(1, limit + 1):\n        if n in found_amicable_numbers:\n            continue\n\n        sum_div_n = calculate_proper_divisor_sum(n)\n\n        if sum_div_n > n and sum_div_n <= limit:\n            sum_div_m = calculate_proper_divisor_sum(sum_div_n)\n\n            if sum_div_m == n:\n                found_amicable_numbers.add(n)\n                found_amicable_numbers.add(sum_div_n)\n\n    total_sum = sum(found_amicable_numbers)\n    return total_sum"}
