{"task_id": "Mbpp/223", "solution": "def _count_occurrences(arr: list[int], n: int, x: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts occurrences of element x in a sorted array arr of length n.\n    Uses binary search to find the first and last occurrences for O(log n) efficiency.\n    \"\"\"\n    first_idx = -1\n    low, high = 0, n - 1\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        if arr[mid] == x:\n            first_idx = mid\n            high = mid - 1\n        elif arr[mid] < x:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid - 1\n\n    if first_idx == -1:\n        return 0\n\n    last_idx = -1\n    low, high = 0, n - 1\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        if arr[mid] == x:\n            last_idx = mid\n            low = mid + 1\n        elif arr[mid] < x:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid - 1\n\n    return last_idx - first_idx + 1\n\ndef _calculate_majority_threshold(n: int) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the majority threshold (n/2).\n    \"\"\"\n    return n / 2.0\n\ndef is_majority(arr: list[int], n: int, x: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if an element x is the majority element in a sorted array arr of length n.\n    A majority element occurs more than n/2 times.\n    \"\"\"\n    count = _count_occurrences(arr, n, x)\n    threshold = _calculate_majority_threshold(n)\n    return count > threshold"}
