{"task_id": "Mbpp/247", "solution": "def lps(s: str) -> int:\n    n = len(s)\n\n    # An empty string has an LPS length of 0.\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    # dp[i][j] stores the length of the longest palindromic subsequence of the substring s[i...j].\n    dp = [[0] * n for _ in range(n)]\n\n    # All single characters are palindromic subsequences of length 1.\n    for i in range(n):\n        dp[i][i] = 1\n\n    # Fill the DP table for substrings of increasing length.\n    for length in range(2, n + 1):\n        for i in range(n - length + 1):\n            j = i + length - 1\n            if s[i] == s[j]:\n                # If the characters at the ends match, they contribute 2 to the LPS length,\n                # plus the LPS of the inner substring s[i+1...j-1].\n                dp[i][j] = 2 + (dp[i + 1][j - 1] if length > 2 else 0)\n            else:\n                # If characters don't match, the LPS is the maximum of excluding s[i] or excluding s[j].\n                dp[i][j] = max(dp[i + 1][j], dp[i][j - 1])\n\n    return dp[0][n - 1]"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/255", "solution": "```python\ndef combinations_colors(input_list: list, n: int) -> list[tuple]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Generates all combinations (with repetition) of the elements of the input_list\n    for a specified length n.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return [()]\n    if not input_list:\n        return []\n\n    result = []\n    for element in input_list:\n        # Recursively generate combinations for n-1 length\n        for sub_combination in combinations_colors(input_list, n - 1):\n            # Prepend the current element to each sub-combination\n            result.append((element,) + sub_combination)\n    return result\n```"}
