{"task_id": "Mbpp/256", "solution": "def count_Primes_nums(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of prime numbers strictly less than the given non-negative number.\n    Uses a helper function _is_prime to determine if a number is prime.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _is_prime(num: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if a given number is prime.\"\"\"\n        if num < 2:\n            return False\n        i = 2\n        while i * i <= num:\n            if num % i == 0:\n                return False\n            i += 1\n        return True\n\n    if number < 2:\n        return 0\n\n    prime_count = 0\n    for num in range(2, number):\n        if _is_prime(num):\n            prime_count += 1\n    return prime_count"}
