{"task_id": "Mbpp/259", "solution": "def maximize_elements(\n    tuple1: tuple[tuple[int, int], ...],\n    tuple2: tuple[tuple[int, int], ...]\n) -> tuple[tuple[int, int], ...]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes a new tuple of tuples where each inner tuple contains the element-wise maximum\n    of corresponding inner tuples from two input tuples.\n    \"\"\"\n    result_list = []\n    for inner_tuple1, inner_tuple2 in zip(tuple1, tuple2):\n        max_elem0 = max(inner_tuple1[0], inner_tuple2[0])\n        max_elem1 = max(inner_tuple1[1], inner_tuple2[1])\n        result_list.append((max_elem0, max_elem1))\n    return tuple(result_list)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/260", "solution": "def newman_prime(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Finds the nth Newman-Shanks-Williams prime number according to the problem's example.\"\"\"\n\n    # Helper function to determine if a number is prime.\n    def is_prime(num: int) -> bool:\n        if num < 2:\n            return False\n        if num == 2:\n            return True\n        if num % 2 == 0:\n            return False\n        i = 3\n        while i * i <= num:\n            if num % i == 0:\n                return False\n            i += 2\n        return True\n\n    # Helper function to calculate the k-th term of the Newman-Shanks-Williams sequence (S_k).\n    def _calculate_nsw_term(k: int) -> int:\n        if k == 0:\n            return 1\n        if k == 1:\n            return 1\n        \n        s_k_minus_2 = 1  # Corresponds to S_0\n        s_k_minus_1 = 1  # Corresponds to S_1\n        \n        for _ in range(2, k + 1):\n            current_s_k = 2 * s_k_minus_1 + s_k_minus_2\n            s_k_minus_2 = s_k_minus_1\n            s_k_minus_1 = current_s_k\n            \n        return s_k_minus_1 # This will be S_k\n\n    # The problem's assert `newman_prime(3) == 7` aligns with `S_3 = 7`.\n    # This implies that the function returns S_n, assuming S_n is the desired prime.\n    \n    nsw_term_n = _calculate_nsw_term(n)\n    \n    return nsw_term_n"}
