{"task_id": "Mbpp/265", "solution": "def list_split(input_list: list, n: int) -> list[list]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Splits an input list into n sublists, distributing elements based on their original index modulo n.\n    Elements at index i are placed into the sublist at index i % n.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 0:\n        # Handle the case where n is non-positive, though the prompt implies valid n\n        return [[]] * len(input_list) if n == 0 else []\n\n    # Initialize n empty sublists\n    sublists = [[] for _ in range(n)]\n\n    # Iterate through the input list with index and element\n    for i, element in enumerate(input_list):\n        # Determine which sublist the current element belongs to\n        target_sublist_index = i % n\n        # Append the element to the calculated sublist\n        sublists[target_sublist_index].append(element)\n\n    return sublists"}
