{"task_id": "Mbpp/235", "solution": "def even_bit_set_number(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sets all even-indexed bits (0-indexed from the right-most bit) of a given integer to 1.\n    This function handles both positive and negative integers within Python's standard arbitrary-precision integer representation.\n    \"\"\"\n    # The mask for setting even bits is a repeating pattern of ...1010101_2, which is 0x55... in hexadecimal.\n    # Python's arbitrary-precision integers and bitwise operations handle masks effectively for all sizes and signs.\n    even_bits_mask = 0x5555555555555555555555555555555555555555555555555555555555555555\n    return number | even_bits_mask"}
