{"task_id": "Mbpp/286", "solution": "def max_sub_array_sum_repeated(arr: list[int], k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the largest sum of a contiguous subarray in the modified array formed by repeating the given array k times.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _kadane(arr: list[int]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Applies Kadane's algorithm to find the maximum contiguous subarray sum in a single array.\"\"\"\n        if not arr:\n            return 0\n\n        max_so_far = arr[0]\n        current_max = arr[0]\n\n        for i in range(1, len(arr)):\n            current_max = max(arr[i], current_max + arr[i])\n            max_so_far = max(max_so_far, current_max)\n        return max_so_far\n\n    n = len(arr)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if k == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    # Case 1: k = 1, or max subarray is contained within one repetition\n    max_sum_single = _kadane(arr)\n    if k == 1:\n        return max_sum_single\n\n    total_sum = sum(arr)\n\n    # Calculate max prefix sum\n    max_prefix_sum = 0\n    current_prefix_sum = 0\n    for x in arr:\n        current_prefix_sum += x\n        max_prefix_sum = max(max_prefix_sum, current_prefix_sum)\n\n    # Calculate max suffix sum\n    max_suffix_sum = 0\n    current_suffix_sum = 0\n    for i in range(n - 1, -1, -1):\n        current_suffix_sum += arr[i]\n        max_suffix_sum = max(max_suffix_sum, current_suffix_sum)\n\n    # Case 2: Max subarray spans across two repetitions (or one plus a full block if total_sum is negative)\n    # This covers subarrays that span the boundary between two copies.\n    max_across_two = max_prefix_sum + max_suffix_sum\n\n    # Case 3: Max subarray spans across more than two repetitions,\n    # or takes advantage of positive total_sum from middle blocks.\n    if total_sum > 0:\n        return max(max_sum_single, max_across_two + (k - 2) * total_sum)\n    else:\n        # If total_sum is negative or zero, adding more full blocks won't increase the sum.\n        # The maximum will be either within a single block or span two blocks.\n        return max(max_sum_single, max_across_two)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/290", "solution": "from typing import List, Any, Tuple\n\ndef max_length(list_of_lists: List[List[Any]]) -> Tuple[int, List[Any]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the list of maximum length in a list of lists.\n    \"\"\"\n    max_len = 0\n    max_sublist: List[Any] = []\n\n    if not list_of_lists:\n        return max_len, max_sublist\n\n    for sublist in list_of_lists:\n        current_len = len(sublist)\n        if current_len > max_len:\n            max_len = current_len\n            max_sublist = sublist\n    return max_len, max_sublist"}
