{"task_id": "Mbpp/311", "solution": "def set_left_most_unset_bit(input_integer: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Identifies the leftmost unset bit in the input_integer and returns a new integer\n    with that bit set to 1. The search considers bits up to and including the position\n    immediately to the left of the most significant set bit (MSB).\n    \"\"\"\n    # Determine the position of the Most Significant Set Bit (MSB).\n    # For input_integer = 0, bit_length() is 0, resulting in msb_pos = -1.\n    msb_pos = input_integer.bit_length() - 1\n\n    # Scan from the MSB position downwards to find the first unset bit.\n    for i in range(msb_pos, -1, -1):\n        if not (input_integer >> i) & 1:  # If the bit at position 'i' is 0\n            return input_integer | (1 << i)  # Set this bit and return.\n\n    # If the loop completes, it means all bits from msb_pos down to 0 are set.\n    # In this case (or if input_integer was 0), the target unset bit is at msb_pos + 1.\n    return input_integer | (1 << (msb_pos + 1))"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/388", "solution": "def highest_Power_of_2(n):\n    power = 1\n    while (power << 1) <= n:\n        power <<= 1\n    return power"}
