{"task_id": "Mbpp/458", "solution": "class Rectangle:\n    \"\"\"Represents a rectangle with length and width, providing area calculation.\n    It validates that dimensions are numeric and non-negative upon initialization.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, length: float, width: float):\n        if not isinstance(length, (int, float)) or not isinstance(width, (int, float)):\n            raise TypeError(\"Length and width must be numeric.\")\n        if length < 0 or width < 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"Length and width must be non-negative.\")\n        self._length = float(length)\n        self._width = float(width)\n\n    def calculate_area(self) -> float:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the area of the rectangle.\"\"\"\n        return self._length * self._width\n\ndef rectangle_area(length: float, width: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the area of a rectangle given its length and width.\n    This function performs input validation and uses the Rectangle class for calculation.\n    \"\"\"\n    rectangle_obj = Rectangle(length, width)\n    return rectangle_obj.calculate_area()"}
