{"task_id": "Mbpp/589", "solution": "import math\n\ndef perfect_squares(lower_bound: int, upper_bound: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Identifies all perfect squares within the inclusive range [lower_bound, upper_bound].\n    Returns a list of perfect squares in ascending order.\n    \"\"\"\n    if lower_bound > upper_bound:\n        return []\n\n    result = []\n    start_sqrt = math.ceil(math.sqrt(max(1, lower_bound)))\n    end_sqrt = math.floor(math.sqrt(upper_bound))\n\n    for i in range(int(start_sqrt), int(end_sqrt) + 1):\n        square = i * i\n        if lower_bound <= square <= upper_bound:\n            result.append(square)\n    return result"}
