{"task_id": "Mbpp/620", "solution": "def largest_subset(numbers: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the size of the largest divisible subset from a given list of numbers.\n    The dynamic programming approach is used for efficiency after sorting the input list.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not numbers:\n        return 0\n\n    # Sort the input list for the dynamic programming approach.\n    # This ensures that if a % b == 0, then b must come before a in the sorted list.\n    numbers.sort()\n\n    n = len(numbers)\n    # dp[i] will store the size of the largest divisible subset ending with numbers[i].\n    dp = [1] * n\n\n    max_size = 1\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i):\n            # Check if numbers[i] is divisible by numbers[j]\n            # Since the list is sorted, numbers[j] <= numbers[i]\n            # so we only need to check numbers[i] % numbers[j] == 0\n            if numbers[i] % numbers[j] == 0:\n                dp[i] = max(dp[i], 1 + dp[j])\n        max_size = max(max_size, dp[i])\n\n    return max_size"}
