{"task_id": "Mbpp/626", "solution": "def triangle_area(radius: float) -> float | None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the area of the largest triangle that can be inscribed in a semicircle.\n    Returns None if the radius is negative.\n    \"\"\"\n    if radius < 0:\n        return None\n    \n    # The largest triangle inscribed in a semicircle has its base along the diameter\n    # and its apex at any point on the arc. The maximum height is the radius itself.\n    base = 2 * radius\n    height = radius\n    area = 0.5 * base * height\n    return area"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/622", "solution": "def get_median(list1: list[int], list2: list[int], n: int) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the median of two sorted lists of the same size.\n    It finds the (n-1)-th and n-th elements of the merged sorted lists.\n    \"\"\"\n    i = 0  # Current index for list1\n    j = 0  # Current index for list2\n    m1 = -1  # Stores the (n-1)-th element (0-indexed)\n    m2 = -1  # Stores the n-th element (0-indexed)\n\n    # Iterate n+1 times to find the (n-1)-th and n-th elements (0-indexed)\n    # which correspond to the n-th and (n+1)-th elements (1-indexed)\n    for _ in range(n + 1):\n        if i == n:  # All elements of list1 have been considered\n            m1 = m2\n            m2 = list2[j]\n            j += 1\n        elif j == n:  # All elements of list2 have been considered\n            m1 = m2\n            m2 = list1[i]\n            i += 1\n        elif list1[i] <= list2[j]:\n            m1 = m2\n            m2 = list1[i]\n            i += 1\n        else:  # list2[j] < list1[i]\n            m1 = m2\n            m2 = list2[j]\n            j += 1\n\n    return (m1 + m2) / 2.0"}
