{"task_id": "Mbpp/721", "solution": "def maxAverageOfPath(matrix: list[list[int]]) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum average path in a square matrix.\n    A path starts from the top-left cell, moves only right or down, and ends on the bottom-right cell.\n    \"\"\"\n    N = len(matrix)\n    \n    # Initialize a DP table to store max total cost to reach each cell.\n    dp = [[0] * N for _ in range(N)]\n\n    # Base case: top-left cell\n    dp[0][0] = matrix[0][0]\n\n    # Fill first row\n    for j in range(1, N):\n        dp[0][j] = dp[0][j - 1] + matrix[0][j]\n\n    # Fill first column\n    for i in range(1, N):\n        dp[i][0] = dp[i - 1][0] + matrix[i][0]\n\n    # Fill the rest of the DP table\n    for i in range(1, N):\n        for j in range(1, N):\n            dp[i][j] = max(dp[i - 1][j], dp[i][j - 1]) + matrix[i][j]\n\n    # The maximum total cost is dp[N-1][N-1].\n    max_total_cost = dp[N - 1][N - 1]\n\n    # The number of cells in any valid path from top-left to bottom-right is (N + N - 1).\n    num_cells = 2 * N - 1\n\n    return max_total_cost / num_cells"}
