{"task_id": "Mbpp/745", "solution": "def _get_digits(number: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Extracts all constituent digits from a given integer number.\n    Converts the number to a string and then to a list of integer digits.\n    \"\"\"\n    return [int(d) for d in str(number)]\n\ndef _is_divisible_by_all_digits(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if a single number is divisible by each of its non-zero constituent digits.\n    Returns False if any digit is zero or if the number is not divisible by a non-zero digit.\n    \"\"\"\n    digits = _get_digits(number)\n    for digit in digits:\n        if digit == 0:\n            return False  # Numbers containing '0' are not considered divisible by '0'\n        if number % digit != 0:\n            return False\n    return True\n\ndef divisible_by_digits(startnum: int, endnum: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds numbers within a given range where every number is divisible by every non-zero digit it contains.\n    Iterates through the range and checks each number using a helper function.\n    \"\"\"\n    result = []\n    for number in range(startnum, endnum + 1):\n        if _is_divisible_by_all_digits(number):\n            result.append(number)\n    return result"}
