{"task_id": "Mbpp/793", "solution": "def last(arr, x):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the last (highest) position of an element in a sorted array using binary search.\n    Returns -1 if the element is not found.\n    \"\"\"\n    low = 0\n    high = len(arr) - 1\n    result = -1\n\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        if arr[mid] == x:\n            result = mid\n            low = mid + 1  # Search in the right half for more occurrences\n        elif arr[mid] < x:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:  # arr[mid] > x\n            high = mid - 1\n    return result"}
